Notebook[{Cell["SignedNegativity", "ObjectName", ExpressionUUID -> "c5ae7c30-43c8-475d-a684-e7e8f5d8002b"], Cell["SignedNegativity[scen, e] gives the negativity of the empirical model e: the minimal total negative weight of a quasi-probability distribution over deterministic global assignments that reproduces e (an exact L1-minimization LP, min (Sum|c|-1)/2 subject to M.c = e). It is 0 exactly when e is noncontextual, and equals CF = 0 iff SignedNegativity = 0. This is a SHEAF-LEVEL resource measure of the empirical model, distinct from the Wigner negativity of a state. The relation to the contextual fraction is scenario-dependent, NOT universal: on the n-cycle CF = (n-1)*SignedNegativity for both the quantum-maximal and Wright models (so the pentagon identity CF = 4 nu is the n = 5 case), while the CHSH PR box and GHZ give CF/nu = 2.", "Usage", ExpressionUUID -> "bcdb1ae3-75a9-4f65-b554-7e744131d4cc"], Cell["Basic Examples", "Section", ExpressionUUID -> "ad49a3e8-ccd0-4e84-a70c-1594d5e601b8"], Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"SignedNegativity", "[", RowBox[{RowBox[{"CycleScenario", "[", "5", "]"}], ",", RowBox[{"CycleModel", "[", RowBox[{"5", ",", "\"Wright\""}], "]"}]}], "]"}]], "Input", ExpressionUUID -> "8da9a67c-6f7c-457d-b367-f509a5d3553a"]}, FrontEndVersion -> "15.0 for Microsoft Windows (64-bit) (May 19, 2026)", StyleDefinitions -> "Default.nb", ExpressionUUID -> "8fbc1ed7-1ecd-4fda-a71a-def5d2696403"]
(* End of Notebook Content *)
